Classic Handbook
Copyright (c) 2026 Classic Handbook. All rights reserved.

Thanks for using Classic Handbook! It's free to use, and it's made with a lot of care, so please don't copy it.

You're welcome to:
- download, install and use Classic Handbook (the program, the Windows app and the website) for free;
- link to it, share screenshots, stream or record it, and write or talk about it.

Please ask first before you:
- copy, redistribute or re-upload the program, the app or the website, or parts of them;
- change it, rebrand it, or pass it off as your own;
- reuse its code, design or layout to make another app or website.

If you'd like to use something, just ask: https://github.com/nairck/ClassicHandbook/issues
I'm happy to hear ideas and requests.

Using Classic Handbook's work:
Classic Handbook is built by hand and checked every day. Our own work is the EXP and mesos model and its estimates,
the price estimates worked out from many sources, the tracker statistics from shared sessions, the compiled data as
we put it together, and how it's all presented. From 18 November 2026 it's shared on these terms. It's no longer
offered under a Creative Commons licence.

Free, no need to ask:
- look things up here by hand;
- a few individual checks a day, by hand or with a small tool of your own, for your own play;
- link to us;
- quote a figure, with credit ("Classic Handbook") and a link.

Needs our written consent first:
- any automated, bulk, regular or repeated collection of our pages or data;
- copying our data, estimates or statistics into another tool, site, bot, spreadsheet, dataset or app;
- using it to train or tune any AI or machine-learning model.

To ask: open an issue at github.com/nairck/ClassicHandbook/issues and say what you'd like to do. We're glad to hear
from fellow players and tool makers.

What isn't ours, and stays under its own terms:
- MapleStory's names, art and game data belong to Nexon. Classic Handbook is an unofficial fan tool, not affiliated
  with or endorsed by Nexon.
- Game data from OSMS Data Explorer is CC BY 4.0.
- Price posts belong to their posters and the sites they're on (credited in the app).
- The share-alike parts: the drop rates measured by MapleClassic Wiki's kill tests, the NPC shop prices from its shop
  pages, and the parts of our drop record built from them are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, as that licence requires. Our consent
  terms don't cover those parts. They can be reused under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, with credit to MapleClassic Wiki and
  Classic Handbook.
- Copies of our data published before 18 November 2026 remain under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

We hold ourselves to the same standard: we read other sites only where their rules allow it, gently, and credit every
one.

